   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general business law, in relation to prohibiting the sale\nof sodium nitrate and sodium nitrite to any person under the age of twenty-one",
    "basePrintNo": "S582",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S582-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 20,
       "fullName": "Zellnor Myrie",
       "imgName": "1048_Zellnor_Myrie.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1228,
       "sessionMemberId": 2025,
       "sessionYear": 2023,
       "shortName": "MYRIE"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §399-hhh, Gen Bus L",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S582\n\nSPONSOR: HOYLMAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to prohibiting the\nsale of sodium nitrate and sodium nitrite to any person under the age of\ntwenty-one\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo prevent the sale of sodium nitrite to individuals under the age of 21\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 creates a new section of the General Business Law to prohibit\nthe sale of sodium nitrate or sodium nitrite to individuals under the\nage of 2, requires businesses to check ID for the sale of sodium nitrate\nor sodium nitrite, and creates a fine of up to $250 for a first offense\nor $500 for subsequent offenses.\n\nSection 2 of the bill is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSodium nitrite is a food additive commonly used to cure meats and poul-\ntry, but it can also be a fatal poison. It is also increasingly used as\na tool for self-harm and suicide. For example, actor Matthew Mindler\nused sodium nitrate bought for $15 on Amazon to commit suicide. Suicide\nrates have increased among all age groups since 2009, but no group has\nsuffered a greater percentage increase in that period than those ages 15\nto 24, among whom the rate has risen 45%.  According to the World Health\nOrganization, suicide is the fourth leading cause of death among 15-19\nyear-olds.  This bill will prohibit the sale of sodium nitrate and sodi-\num nitrite to those under 21, and it will require ID checks for anyone\nthat appears to be under the age of 30.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS.7601 of 2021-2022 (Hoylman): Died in Consumer Protection\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect thirty days after it shall have become a law.\n",
